# sandbox/canaries.sha256: canary tokens by hash (DV4-PLAN §5.4 item 2).
# One line per canary: the sha256 of the full token (the public prefix
# DVLCANARY- and a random suffix), two spaces, and the tree it marks. The
# sandbox self-test refuses any staged file that carries the public prefix and
# names the tree by the token's hash, so a study-mode run needs no secret and
# reads no reference tree. Planted by the DV5c gaps lane (DV4-PLAN §14 Q5):
# one file named DVLCANARY at the top of each reference tree, the hidden
# truth, the author cache and each public set's answers/ (the last written by
# scripts/get_bench.sh from the set's name and pinned commit, outside the
# set's digest). The token is the file's first line; nothing else is secret.
# A line whose tree is a sealed archive (*.tar.age) marks a canary planted INSIDE the
# archive's plaintext (topic (e)'s sealed references, DELTAS Δ409): a staged file that
# carries it was copied out of a sealed reference.
